   ],
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "key",
     "style": "definition",
     "title": "Loops",
     "md": "**FOR** repeats a known number of times. **WHILE** repeats while a condition is true (it may not run at all). **REPEAT ... UNTIL** runs at least once. Be sure the condition can become false, otherwise the loop never ends."
    },
    {
     "type": "key",
     "style": "retenir",
     "title": "Lists (arrays)",
     "md": "A **list** (array) stores several values of the same type under one name, with an **index**: marks[1], marks[2], ... (this course starts at 1). A FOR loop is a good way to process every item: total = total + marks[i]."
    },
